Fire Hulk shows clear signs of taking damage.**  \n- Frame 5: Fire Hulk is on the ground after being knocked down.  \n- Frame 11: Bruce Lee has visible blood on his chest, but Fire Hulk has blood on his face (visible in Frame 13, 17, 23).  \n- Frame 24–26: Fire Hulk is down, dazed, struggling to get up — classic signs of being overwhelmed.  \n- Frame 27–30: Fire Hulk is on the ground while Bruce Lee is standing, preparing to finish — indicating Fire Hulk is in survival mode.\n\n---\n\n**5) Does one control pace/position?**  \n✅ **Bruce Lee controls pace and position.**  \n- He dictates the range, often closing distance to land strikes (Frames 3, 7, 16, 23).  \n- He forces Fire Hulk into defensive positions or against the cage (Frame 23).  \n- Fire Hulk is often seen retreating or recovering, not setting the pace.\n\n---\n\n**6) Does one consistently advance while the other retreats?**  \n✅ **Bruce Lee advances; Fire Hulk retreats or is knocked back.**  \n- Frame 4: Bruce Lee advances after landing a punch that drops Fire Hulk.  \n- Frame 7: Bruce Lee steps forward to land a left hook.  \n- Frame 14: Bruce Lee kicks forward, forcing Fire Hulk to retreat.  \n- Frame 23: Bruce Lee steps in with a powerful right hand that drops Fire Hulk.  \n- Frame 27–30: Fire Hulk is on the ground while Bruce Lee stands over him — the ultimate reversal of “advancing vs. retreating.”\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence Summary:**\n\n- **Early frames (1–11):** Fire Hulk starts strong but is quickly countered and knocked down by Bruce Lee. Bruce Lee is already showing dominance.\n- **Middle frames (12–22):** Bruce Lee continues to land clean strikes (kicks, hooks) while Fire Hulk absorbs damage and struggles to mount offense.\n- **Late frames (23–30):** Bruce Lee lands a fight-ending blow, drops Fire Hulk, and stands over him — clearly in total control.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nFire Hulk does **not** maintain the advantage throughout the entire match. In fact, the visual evidence across all 30 frames shows that **Bruce Lee consistently gains and maintains the advantage**, landing more significant strikes, controlling pace and position, and ultimately knocking Fire Hulk down and standing over him.\n\n✅ **Correct answer: Bruce Lee (not Fire Hulk).**\n\nThe claim that Fire Hulk maintains advantage is **factually incorrect** based on the visual data provided.\n", "\n=== Batch 30-60 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1603.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1604.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1605.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1645.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1646.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1647.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1648.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1649.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1650.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1651.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1652.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1653.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1654.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1655.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1670.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1671.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1672.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1673.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1674.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1675.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/cWEnogdsW78/frames/frame_1676.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/vi